-- §3 `inst` selection at two DIFFERENT FUNCTION-TYPED impl heads — the #1617 DRAIN.
--
-- This is the permanent home of `test/must_fail_fixtures/1617-fn-typed-impl-head-
-- none-bucket/`, which pinned the BROKEN behaviour and drained when the fix landed.
-- A must-fail row asserts a bug STILL REPRODUCES and cannot coexist with a row
-- asserting it is fixed, so the shape moves here rather than being deleted — same
-- migration `s3-nary-requires-goal-vector.mdk` made for #1154 and
-- `s3-min-fully-general-sibling.mdk` for #1128 (the neighbouring `noneHeadTag` drain).
--
-- WAS: `headTyconTy` (compiler/types/typecheck.mdk) answered None for anything that
-- is not a `TyCon` and not a `TyTuple` — `TyFun` included, although the arm is
-- documented as "a type VARIABLE head has no head tycon". Both heads landed in the
-- ONE `noneHeadTag` bucket and could not be discriminated: `check` was clean at
-- exit 0, `run` answered by DECLARATION ORDER (this ordering printed `(5, 5)`; the
-- reversed one printed `(9, 9)`), and `build` exited 1 with
--   runtime error [E-PANIC]: arg-tag dispatch on impl type that owns no
--   constructors (primitive receiver carries no cell tag)
--
-- HAND-DERIVED CORRECT ANSWER, from the source, not from the binary:
--   `sz f` — f : Int -> Int   -> the `impl Sz (Int -> Int)` body  -> 5
--   `sz g` — g : Bool -> Bool -> the `impl Sz (Bool -> Bool)` body -> 9
--   so this prints `(5, 9)`, on run AND on the shipped binary (§7 value agreement).
--
-- ⚠️ THE VALUE ROW ALONE IS NOT THE WHOLE ASSERTION, AND THAT IS WHY THIS FIXTURE
-- IS A FLAT `.mdk` AND NOT A DIRECTORY. Section 4 derives its permutation set from
-- `test/dict_fixtures/*.mdk` with >=2 `impl` blocks of one interface, so this file
-- is automatically permuted: reversing the two `impl Sz` blocks must not change
-- `check`'s verdict, `run`'s stdout or `build`'s stdout. That is the half the
-- drained must-fail fixture could only carry as an UNGRADED third file
-- (`permutation.mdk`, run by nothing) — here it EXECUTES. It is also the half that
-- matters most: the defect's signature was a declaration-order-dependent wrong
-- answer, and a value pin alone passes by construction on the order it was
-- captured at.
--
-- ⚠️ NOT #1180 (`headTyconTy`'s bare-`TyVar` arm, where answering None is the
-- documented intent and the program must be REJECTED) and NOT #1630 (the same
-- `_ => None` arm set at a headed `TyConstrained` body — `impl Sz (Eq a => Int)`,
-- still `check=0 run=0 build=1` on this binary). The `_ => None` arm set is not
-- finished; this row is the executable memory that THIS member of it was repaired.
interface Sz a where
  sz : a -> Int

impl Sz (Int -> Int) where
  sz _ = 5

impl Sz (Bool -> Bool) where
  sz _ = 9

f : Int -> Int
f x = x + 1

g : Bool -> Bool
g b = b

main = println (sz f, sz g)
